  "note": "Time and wall baselines are per CPU model. EPYC 7763 stays the two-sweep confirmation from run 44210506592 (median 208, margin 0.043); later VMs of that model were not folded in, because that would widen the margin, and the top-level medians and the ratio ceiling stay tied to that run. EPYC 9V74 (7 VMs), EPYC 9V45 (5 VMs), and Xeon 6975P-C (5 VMs) are the median of per-VM medians. Each VM median is five fresh processes. The margin is max(5 * largest within-VM CV, 2 * |min/max - 1|), rounded up to the next 0.001. ci95 on those rows is the 95% CI of the mean of the VM medians (df = VMs - 1) and is not the limit. Xeon Platinum 8573C stays the single-run row from run 44213844582. Xeon 6973P-C was seen on two VMs and has no row. An unknown model fails the job. RSS margins 0.109 and 0.003 and the endpoint-ratio ceiling 46.67056578947369 are unchanged."
